WEBVTT

00:02.440 --> 00:04.980
Ron! Are you in?

00:04.980 --> 00:06.990
<i>Shooting Star Viewing</i>

00:07.820 --> 00:09.280
Hey, Toto.

00:09.910 --> 00:10.870
Do you have a case?

00:11.170 --> 00:12.830
The hell is with your eyes, Ron?!

00:12.830 --> 00:15.290
Seriously, your eyes... What happened?

00:16.610 --> 00:19.120
I've gotten addicted to that modern marvel.

00:21.460 --> 00:25.340
It's packed with people and scenery 
and dreams. What a magnificent slab it is.

00:25.340 --> 00:27.340
You can just call it a TV!

00:27.340 --> 00:30.260
Psychic Abilities: Fact or Fiction?

00:27.590 --> 00:31.540
Daba, doobie-doo, daba-doobie-doo, baya!

00:28.280 --> 00:30.260
<i>Psychic Abilities: Fact or Fiction?</i>

00:31.540 --> 00:35.440
Daba, doobie-doo, daba-doobie-doo, baya!

00:48.250 --> 00:51.570
Ron    Kamonohashi's

00:48.250 --> 00:51.570
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

02:05.980 --> 02:08.980
Psychic Abilities:
Fact or Fiction?

02:09.020 --> 02:13.450
<b>#06   The Case of the Live Broadcast Murder</b>

02:09.210 --> 02:13.450
Let's start the live broadcast of 
<i>Psychic Abilities: Fact or Fiction?</i>

02:13.890 --> 02:15.910
I'm Ono Yako, your host.

02:16.460 --> 02:20.160
On our show, a psychic and a
 neurosurgeon go head to head

02:20.160 --> 02:22.620
in an attempt to verify psychic powers.

02:23.010 --> 02:25.020
The one demonstrating their power

02:24.670 --> 02:26.830
<b>Psychic
Torage Dankichi</b>

02:25.020 --> 02:26.830
is a psychic you all know, Torage-san!

02:29.300 --> 02:33.880
And up against him is the genius 
neurosurgeon with miraculous hands...

02:31.800 --> 02:34.260
<b>Neurosurgeon
Usaki Mofu</b>

02:33.880 --> 02:34.750
Oh.

02:35.160 --> 02:36.970
Mofu-sensei, the show has started!

02:36.970 --> 02:39.050
What? Already?

02:39.050 --> 02:41.010
Please look toward the camera.

02:42.930 --> 02:44.630
Is she severely injured?!

02:45.160 --> 02:46.630
She's got more bandages again.

02:46.630 --> 02:47.270
Huh?

02:47.270 --> 02:49.230
Oh, I'm so sorry.

02:49.230 --> 02:51.000
Doctor, what happened to your face?

02:51.000 --> 02:54.300
I was cutting an apple 
and the knife sprang back at me.

02:54.300 --> 02:56.700
Sorry, I'm really bad at wrapping bandages.

02:58.160 --> 03:01.440
Mofu-sensei is odd,
so she's lots of fun to watch.

03:01.440 --> 03:04.150
Is she really a genius surgeon?

03:04.150 --> 03:10.130
Her procedures are accurate to 0.001mm.
She's a globally preeminent super doctor.

03:10.130 --> 03:11.380
<i>Ouch!</i>

03:11.890 --> 03:14.690
I was adjusting my mic 
and it clipped to my chin!

03:14.690 --> 03:15.850
Ow!

03:17.070 --> 03:19.010
How clumsy can you be?!

03:20.350 --> 03:23.600
Well, Torage-san, what sort
of power will you show us today?

03:23.600 --> 03:27.190
The time has finally come to demonstrate 
what I'm truly capable of.

03:27.190 --> 03:30.560
Today, I will show you I can
control a mind using only writing.

03:30.560 --> 03:32.020
What? Huh?

03:32.020 --> 03:33.730
That sounds intriguing!

03:33.730 --> 03:35.260
You can do this, Torage!

03:35.260 --> 03:37.860
Ron, you believe in psychic stuff?

03:37.860 --> 03:39.110
Not at all.

03:39.110 --> 03:41.900
Huh? Then why are you cheering him on?

03:41.900 --> 03:46.110
Because if psychic powers were real, 
solving cases would be more fun.

03:46.110 --> 03:49.080
I'd love to crack even more
 complicated mysteries.

03:50.790 --> 03:54.050
You seem like the gullible type
who'd just shout, "That's amazing!"

03:54.050 --> 03:57.720
I'm not <i>that</i> easily taken in. 
You don't give me enough credit.

03:57.720 --> 04:01.180
If you can resist my psychic influence,

04:01.180 --> 04:04.190
I will reward you with 100,000 yen.

04:04.190 --> 04:05.220
Any volunteers?

04:05.220 --> 04:07.670
Over here!

04:05.220 --> 04:07.670
Me, me!

04:07.670 --> 04:10.440
I'll take you in the white hoodie.

04:10.850 --> 04:13.900
All right! I'm gonna get 
that 100,000 yen!

04:16.610 --> 04:21.570
I will say in advance that what's about 
to happen is not by power of suggestion.

04:22.110 --> 04:25.900
What I write on this card 
will exert direct control of him.

04:26.720 --> 04:31.550
The subject is wearing noise-canceling 
headphones prepared by the staff.

04:31.550 --> 04:33.670
With those on, he can't hear a thing.

04:34.040 --> 04:37.130
Nevertheless, the instant he reads this...

04:42.420 --> 04:44.010
My body's...

04:44.370 --> 04:45.970
Wait, huh? What?!

04:45.970 --> 04:47.370
Huh?!

04:47.370 --> 04:48.180
No way!

04:48.180 --> 04:49.640
That's amazing!

04:49.640 --> 04:52.360
He's doing exactly 
as the card says in English!

04:52.360 --> 04:54.830
Everyone, a round of applause for Torage-san!

04:57.500 --> 04:59.420
This is the next word.

04:59.420 --> 05:03.620
He will heed it and obey
 regardless of his own will.

05:05.140 --> 05:06.020
Huh?

05:06.580 --> 05:07.950
S-Seriously?!

05:07.950 --> 05:10.250
Amazing... Just amazing!

05:10.590 --> 05:12.790
This time, the word "run" 
made him start running!

05:12.790 --> 05:16.220
Is his mind really being controlled
by what's written on these cards?!

05:16.840 --> 05:19.050
Will Mofu-sensei pick up on it?

05:19.050 --> 05:20.130
Huh?

05:22.270 --> 05:24.300
You're mocking neuroscience.

05:24.300 --> 05:26.760
Usaki-sensei will now give her rebuttal!

05:26.760 --> 05:30.730
Was the subject really chosen at random?

05:30.730 --> 05:31.810
What?

05:31.810 --> 05:35.020
Of course. What gives you any doubt?

05:35.400 --> 05:39.130
Just like your fingerprints,
you can't change the way you move.

05:39.490 --> 05:48.450
\h\h\hMatch\h\h\h

05:39.900 --> 05:44.580
I ran the subject through a biological 
motion app that analyzes movement,

05:44.580 --> 05:48.450
and I've determined he's the same
 subject from your last demonstration.

05:49.300 --> 05:51.910
He's a plant in league with you, Torage-san!

05:53.000 --> 05:54.290
So she did notice.

05:54.290 --> 05:55.880
It was all staged?

05:56.620 --> 05:57.940
Here's the proof!

05:57.940 --> 05:59.210
We can't see through the cracks!

05:59.210 --> 06:03.180
I mean, they always get run over by 
dump trucks when you drop them, you know?

06:03.180 --> 06:04.890
I can't say I would...

06:06.100 --> 06:08.240
Kindly refrain from false accusations.

06:09.560 --> 06:15.120
If this next word reaches his brain, 
will you believe he wasn't planted?

06:15.120 --> 06:16.230
What?

06:18.690 --> 06:21.900
The word he's written now
 can only mean one thing!

06:23.610 --> 06:28.330
What do you think, Usaki-sensei? 
If the subject dies, will you believe me?

06:28.330 --> 06:30.290
There's no way this will take his life.

06:30.290 --> 06:31.910
Take that as my answer.

06:32.220 --> 06:35.280
Oh dear. Well then...

06:54.370 --> 06:55.800
He's dead.

06:57.560 --> 06:58.930
Th-This is bad!

06:58.930 --> 06:59.930
Stop the broadcast!

06:59.930 --> 07:01.070
I've called an ambulance!

07:01.430 --> 07:03.320
Cut to the screen we use for accidents!

07:03.320 --> 07:04.820
We'll be right back

07:07.330 --> 07:09.790
It can't be...

07:10.230 --> 07:13.250
This is a live broadcast. We've got 
no time to laze around here.

07:13.250 --> 07:14.260
Yeah.

07:21.630 --> 07:23.350
Oh, Isshiki-san.

07:23.350 --> 07:26.840
We've just confirmed the death 
and secured the scene.

07:27.280 --> 07:28.520
Good work.

07:28.520 --> 07:29.700
Who's that with you?

07:29.700 --> 07:30.300
Huh?

07:30.300 --> 07:32.260
I'm Asasuki Kamoji.

07:32.260 --> 07:32.930
<b>Torage</b>

07:32.990 --> 07:34.750
I'm a bandwagon Torage fan!

07:34.750 --> 07:37.350
You're the worst person to let in here!

07:37.350 --> 07:40.810
He's a specialist helping out
with the investigation!

07:40.810 --> 07:42.500
Excuse me.

07:42.900 --> 07:45.290
Don't worry. I will avenge you.

07:46.190 --> 07:47.530
Who's he?

07:47.700 --> 07:50.490
Oh, Torage-kun! I saw you on TV!

07:50.490 --> 07:51.870
And you are?

07:51.870 --> 07:53.830
I'm a bandwagon fan!

07:53.830 --> 07:56.290
Nix the "bandwagon" bit! And get up!

07:56.290 --> 07:58.490
What's a fan doing here?

07:58.490 --> 07:59.650
I'm so sorry.

07:59.650 --> 08:02.250
I wanted to ask you something, Torage-kun.

08:02.250 --> 08:04.630
D-Don't say anything rude.

08:04.630 --> 08:06.340
How'd you kill him?

08:06.340 --> 08:08.050
That's majorly rude!

08:08.050 --> 08:09.660
But you gotta ask, right?

08:09.660 --> 08:11.360
No, you don't!

08:11.360 --> 08:12.760
You're amusing.

08:12.760 --> 08:15.970
I killed him with my psychic powers.

08:17.180 --> 08:22.160
But under modern science and the law, 
I cannot be held accountable.

08:22.160 --> 08:24.150
You admit that you killed him?

08:24.910 --> 08:28.490
<i>Except I can't arrest a guy
for a psychically-induced death.</i>

08:28.490 --> 08:30.950
I knew it! You really are the best!

08:32.230 --> 08:33.640
Can I have your autograph?

08:33.950 --> 08:35.410
That's my notebook!

08:35.710 --> 08:37.620
On that tiny paper?

08:37.620 --> 08:39.690
Well, this is all so sudden.

08:39.690 --> 08:43.090
Do you have a pen? The one you 
used on those cards would be fine.

08:43.590 --> 08:44.590
What?

08:45.800 --> 08:47.780
Once I've signed this, begone.

08:51.250 --> 08:52.680
It's so thick I can't read it.

08:52.680 --> 08:54.420
He's pissed at you!

08:54.420 --> 08:58.270
If that neurosurgeon had 
only believed in psychic powers,

08:58.270 --> 09:01.260
this demonstration would have
 been unnecessary.

09:01.260 --> 09:02.850
If anyone's to be punished,

09:02.850 --> 09:05.570
it should be her, don't you think?

09:06.260 --> 09:07.800
No way...

09:10.990 --> 09:13.200
We'll be right back

09:18.430 --> 09:22.210
I'm Shikata, Usaki-sensei's
 assistant at the hospital.

09:22.210 --> 09:25.210
The doctor's beside herself right now.

09:25.210 --> 09:28.670
I don't think what happened here
 was her fault.

09:28.670 --> 09:30.070
No...

09:30.070 --> 09:32.130
I'm a practitioner of medicine.

09:32.610 --> 09:36.600
I have to take responsibility for allowing 
someone to die right in front of me!

09:38.060 --> 09:43.520
Mofu-sensei, has this incident 
made you believe in psychic powers?

09:43.520 --> 09:45.210
I don't know.

09:45.210 --> 09:48.980
I examined the body and 
the cause of death was poison.

09:49.720 --> 09:50.890
Poison?

09:50.890 --> 09:55.340
I observed flaccid paralysis, 
and given the presentation of cyanosis,

09:55.340 --> 09:57.450
I believe it was a neurotoxin.

09:58.210 --> 10:00.650
Blowfish poison or snake venom, or...

10:01.010 --> 10:04.350
He went into cardiac arrest
before the ambulance arrived,

10:04.720 --> 10:07.420
so it may have been 
the potent botulinum toxin.

10:07.820 --> 10:09.870
My thoughts precisely.

10:09.870 --> 10:11.840
I'd expect no less of you, Mofu-sensei.

10:11.840 --> 10:14.520
I figured that speck 
on the back of the victim's neck

10:14.520 --> 10:17.030
might be a mark left by a poisoned needle.

10:17.030 --> 10:18.180
What do you think?

10:18.180 --> 10:20.020
I thought exactly the same thing!

10:20.020 --> 10:21.420
Great minds, huh?

10:21.960 --> 10:23.730
Are you a medical doctor?

10:23.730 --> 10:25.060
I'm a Torage fan.

10:25.060 --> 10:28.020
You don't have to be <i>that</i> stupidly honest!

10:28.020 --> 10:30.000
If there's a mark from a poisoned needle,

10:30.000 --> 10:33.320
does that mean Torage used 
a blowgun or something to stab him?

10:33.720 --> 10:35.630
I'm afraid not.

10:35.630 --> 10:38.500
He didn't do anything that seemed suspicious.

10:38.500 --> 10:40.890
And from where he was standing,
 he couldn't have hit the subject.

10:40.890 --> 10:44.870
Moreover, there wasn't 
anyone behind the subject!

10:44.870 --> 10:47.750
No matter how I rack my brain,
I can't explain it!

10:47.750 --> 10:50.460
You're right. It was a superhuman feat.

10:50.460 --> 10:52.960
The only explanation is psychic powers.

10:52.960 --> 10:55.930
Yay! Torage-san for the win! Fans rejoice!

10:55.930 --> 10:57.890
You really are the worst, you know that?

10:59.850 --> 11:03.520
Mofu-sensei has a personal reason
 she can't be bested here.

11:04.310 --> 11:07.390
It's why she came after
an all-night surgery and

11:07.390 --> 11:09.770
forced herself to participate
 in today's show.

11:09.770 --> 11:14.240
Then let's solve this case quickly 
so she can get some sleep.

11:15.950 --> 11:20.950
We'll figure out the trick and 
see the fake psychic off the stage.

11:21.350 --> 11:21.950
<i>Ron...</i>

11:22.870 --> 11:24.120
The trick?

11:24.500 --> 11:26.450
It wasn't psychic power.

11:27.100 --> 11:30.450
But you said you were a fan of Torage's...

11:30.450 --> 11:32.500
Just a bandwagon fan.

11:32.500 --> 11:37.010
The only thing I'm a true
 life-long fan of is the truth.

11:37.010 --> 11:42.010
The pure, naïve Detective Isshiki
will expose the trick here.

11:44.840 --> 11:47.650
Just after the subject saw the cue card,

11:47.650 --> 11:50.630
he closed his eyes and 
collapsed to the floor, right?

11:51.060 --> 11:53.860
And after that, he didn't even twitch?

11:53.860 --> 11:54.530
No.

11:55.290 --> 12:00.240
When I was giving him CPR, 
he came to for just a moment.

12:00.240 --> 12:02.130
He was in distress,

12:02.580 --> 12:04.950
then his breathing stopped again.

12:05.520 --> 12:07.840
There's no way Torage stabbed

12:07.840 --> 12:11.510
the subject in the neck
while the doctor was giving him CPR.

12:11.960 --> 12:15.420
Forensics hasn't turned up
 any poisoned needles, either.

12:15.420 --> 12:18.180
It looks like this really was
 caused psychically.

12:18.180 --> 12:21.140
No. We've got all the pieces, Toto.

12:21.140 --> 12:21.900
What?

12:22.570 --> 12:24.600
The entirety of this trick...

12:24.600 --> 12:26.560
is on TV.

12:26.690 --> 12:29.700
You've got hyperemia in your eyes. 
Have some eye drops.

12:29.700 --> 12:31.020
You're so kind.

12:31.020 --> 12:32.620
Take good care of yourself.

12:32.620 --> 12:33.590
Thank you.

12:34.980 --> 12:37.240
<b>Studio 6</b>

12:37.240 --> 12:39.700
Thank you for gathering here.

12:39.700 --> 12:44.770
I will now solve the mystery of how 
the subject died during the show.

12:45.240 --> 12:50.710
And since the stage is still set, 
let's try reenacting the incident.

12:50.710 --> 12:52.180
You want to reenact it?

12:52.180 --> 12:53.670
Can you really do that?

12:54.080 --> 12:57.380
Usaki-sensei, could I ask you
 to play the subject?

12:57.380 --> 12:58.920
Me?

12:59.340 --> 13:01.780
I'll stand in for Torage-san.

13:01.780 --> 13:06.280
To ensure this is accurate, 
I asked the staff for the same cue cards.

13:06.280 --> 13:09.100
Torage-san, could I borrow the pen you used?

13:09.100 --> 13:11.770
There's no need to go that far.

13:11.770 --> 13:14.480
Why should I go along with this farce?

13:14.480 --> 13:16.640
Someone lost their life here!

13:16.640 --> 13:18.150
Please just lend us the pen!

13:24.200 --> 13:25.830
I'm so sorry!

13:25.830 --> 13:28.290
<i>Full-throttle clumsiness on display!</i>

13:30.100 --> 13:32.250
Torage-san, we'll be borrowing this!

13:32.250 --> 13:33.390
Tch.

13:36.670 --> 13:40.050
Usaki-sensei will put on 
the noise-canceling headphones

13:40.050 --> 13:42.380
and act out what's written here.

13:42.380 --> 13:44.470
Basically, she'll do as the plant would.

13:44.470 --> 13:47.880
Hey! Calling him a plant is unfair!

13:47.880 --> 13:49.930
What idiot would die for a staged trick?!

13:49.930 --> 13:53.650
P-Please, calm down! 
That's what we're testing right now.

13:56.600 --> 13:57.570
Now then...

13:58.050 --> 13:59.520
Please start with this word.

14:02.490 --> 14:03.850
Very good.

14:04.460 --> 14:05.950
Now, on to the next word.

14:07.040 --> 14:08.430
Wonderful!

14:08.430 --> 14:10.040
She's following along perfectly.

14:10.040 --> 14:13.560
Well, of course she is.
You're telling her what to do.

14:13.560 --> 14:16.230
This is stupid. Is that detective okay?

14:18.380 --> 14:20.840
Now, at last, the word in question.

14:21.590 --> 14:25.550
I'll have Usaki-sensei stand 
right where the subject was.

14:26.240 --> 14:28.010
I'll show her this the same way, too.

14:35.020 --> 14:36.980
Mofu-sensei!

14:37.730 --> 14:39.690
Please, stay calm!

14:39.690 --> 14:42.170
Usaki-sensei is not dead.

14:42.170 --> 14:44.220
Then what did you do?

14:44.220 --> 14:46.020
Is there some trick to the cue card?

14:46.020 --> 14:48.500
No, it's just regular, extra-thick paper.

14:48.500 --> 14:52.480
But at the time of the incident, 
Torage-san set the card on the podium.

14:52.800 --> 14:56.540
He then turned it upside down 
and showed it to the subject.

14:56.540 --> 14:58.500
He turned it upside down?

15:05.680 --> 15:07.100
Like this.

15:08.390 --> 15:09.800
"Sleep"?!

15:10.240 --> 15:11.060
It says sleep!

15:11.060 --> 15:14.520
Turned upside down, "death" becomes "sleep"?!

15:14.520 --> 15:18.980
Which means that when he collapsed, 
the subject was still conscious?

15:18.980 --> 15:20.360
That's right.

15:20.360 --> 15:23.190
The subject was pretending to be asleep.

15:23.940 --> 15:26.580
The headphones prevented him
 from hearing the commotion,

15:26.580 --> 15:30.490
so he kept up the act even as
Torage-san took his pulse.

15:30.490 --> 15:33.450
So, when was the subject killed?

15:34.270 --> 15:36.270
After the broadcast was suspended,

15:36.270 --> 15:38.350
while standing among the crowd

15:38.350 --> 15:42.460
and amid all the chaos, 
Torage-san injected him with poison!

15:44.170 --> 15:47.740
That means he showed signs
 of distress during CPR

15:47.740 --> 15:50.640
because the injected poison
took time to circulate.

15:51.020 --> 15:53.660
No psychic abilities were used.

15:53.660 --> 15:56.240
Isn't that right, Torage-san?

15:59.470 --> 16:01.700
These accusations are completely unfounded!

16:01.700 --> 16:04.190
First and foremost, you haven't 
found a poisoned needle!

16:04.190 --> 16:06.570
No, we retrieved it.

16:06.570 --> 16:07.870
Wha—?!

16:11.970 --> 16:14.150
When you were asked to sign my notebook,

16:14.150 --> 16:17.620
why did you choose such a thick, unwieldy pen?

16:17.960 --> 16:21.580
Because the poisoned needle was 
hidden inside the tip of your thinner pen!

16:22.790 --> 16:25.010
That's where he concealed it?

16:25.010 --> 16:28.720
You're wrong! This death 
was the result of psychic powers!

16:28.720 --> 16:32.010
If you don't believe me, I'll prove it to you!

16:34.260 --> 16:38.540
Torage Psychic!

16:43.110 --> 16:45.410
I'm lying. I give up.

16:51.090 --> 16:55.370
He was just a plant, 
but he started threatening me!

16:55.370 --> 16:57.550
He said he'd out my tricks

16:57.550 --> 17:00.080
if I didn't fork over 
90 percent of my earnings.

17:00.080 --> 17:02.200
Killing him was my only choice!

17:03.510 --> 17:04.920
Stab yourself.

17:06.130 --> 17:08.840
Anyone who dismisses the lives of others...

17:09.350 --> 17:11.630
has no right to live in this world.

17:12.090 --> 17:13.550
<i>This is bad!</i>

17:13.550 --> 17:15.110
Stab yourself.

17:18.140 --> 17:20.440
Stab... myself...

17:27.730 --> 17:28.900
Stop!

17:45.490 --> 17:46.800
The poisoned needle!

17:50.010 --> 17:51.470
Toto!

17:52.860 --> 17:54.180
Let me take a look!

17:54.530 --> 17:56.070
It's too late!

17:56.640 --> 17:58.200
The mark of the poisoned needle...

17:58.200 --> 17:59.850
Mark of the poisoned needle?

17:59.850 --> 18:02.640
I swapped the pen tip with the needle.

18:02.640 --> 18:04.560
There's no way it'd leave an ink mark.

18:04.560 --> 18:05.310
What?

18:05.850 --> 18:08.020
Then this pen is...

18:15.780 --> 18:18.190
Here it is! 
This one's the poisoned needle pen!

18:27.840 --> 18:31.770
Honestly, Ron. I seriously 
thought I was a dead man.

18:34.280 --> 18:36.670
I'm sorry. I regret what I've done.

18:36.670 --> 18:41.360
You say that now, but later, I know you'll
 ask me for the next case like always.

18:42.120 --> 18:45.480
It was a mistake for me 
to start sleuthing again.

18:45.480 --> 18:48.300
<i>Huh? He's not talking back.</i>

18:48.300 --> 18:51.600
If that had gone any further,
 there'd be no undoing what I wrought.

18:52.440 --> 18:56.160
I have no right to be a detective.

19:00.200 --> 19:02.200
<i>He's really down on himself.</i>

19:02.200 --> 19:04.200
<i>Like back when I first met him.</i>

19:04.770 --> 19:06.830
<i>Not that I don't understand why.</i>

19:07.340 --> 19:11.250
<i>Maybe it's time to give up
this dangerous approach.</i>

19:11.250 --> 19:13.300
Oh, Isshiki-san!

19:15.760 --> 19:18.360
My bandages are caught on the handrail!

19:18.360 --> 19:20.010
That takes skill!

19:20.720 --> 19:23.730
Thank you so much for what you did today.

19:23.730 --> 19:25.230
Don't mention it.

19:25.670 --> 19:29.690
So many patients 
are going to live because of you.

19:30.520 --> 19:33.890
A long time ago, I had a patient 
who believed in psychic treatments,

19:33.890 --> 19:36.490
refused surgery, 
and passed away because of it.

19:36.490 --> 19:38.600
That's why you were trying so hard...

19:39.070 --> 19:43.290
Your brilliant deductions
 will save lots of lives!

19:45.500 --> 19:48.250
Yeah, you're right...

19:48.800 --> 19:51.960
I feel reenergized! Thank you, Mofu-sensei!

19:51.960 --> 19:53.440
Not at all.

19:53.920 --> 19:55.720
I'll be on my way.

19:57.300 --> 20:01.800
Oh, and I'm sorry for giving you
a scare at the end there.

20:01.800 --> 20:05.520
He's got a weird habit of 
pressuring murderers into things.

20:06.200 --> 20:07.610
Pressuring them...?

20:08.350 --> 20:09.870
Well, I'll see you later!

20:12.780 --> 20:16.640
That was more than just pressuring...

20:21.060 --> 20:22.060
Ron!

20:25.200 --> 20:27.660
You can't quit over something like that!

20:28.360 --> 20:29.850
"Something like that"?

20:30.430 --> 20:34.340
I nearly killed you.

20:34.340 --> 20:36.340
It was just an accident.

20:36.340 --> 20:40.530
If anything like it happened again
and you died...

20:41.090 --> 20:44.990
I'd despair of myself and wouldn't 
be able to carry on.

20:44.990 --> 20:48.250
I swear, don't write me off
 as a goner so readily.

20:48.250 --> 20:50.180
Next time, I'll stop you.

20:50.180 --> 20:53.940
So I want you to have some faith 
in Kamonohashi Ron, too!

20:55.400 --> 20:57.470
You love sleuthing above all else.

20:57.470 --> 20:59.660
You've devoted your life
to being a detective.

20:59.660 --> 21:02.130
Why did you shut yourself away
for five years?

21:02.620 --> 21:05.080
It's because you care about people's lives!

21:05.080 --> 21:06.070
Toto...

21:06.070 --> 21:10.080
People's lives are at the core 
of your guiding principles and all you do.

21:10.670 --> 21:12.790
That's just the kind of guy you are.

21:13.830 --> 21:15.250
But...

21:15.250 --> 21:16.540
Oh, right.

21:17.710 --> 21:19.670
<i><b>Shooting Star Viewing</b></i>

21:20.760 --> 21:22.140
An invitation?

21:29.310 --> 21:34.000
A gathering at an observatory on a remote 
island to watch the Leonid meteor shower?

21:34.000 --> 21:35.240
What is this?

21:35.240 --> 21:36.750
It arrived this morning.

21:36.750 --> 21:39.480
I don't know the sender very well,

21:39.480 --> 21:42.260
but times like this call for a change of pace.

21:42.260 --> 21:46.530
Until you can believe in yourself, 
I'll stick with you! Okay?

21:48.640 --> 21:50.300
You're right.

21:50.300 --> 21:53.710
It might be good to get away from mysteries.

21:54.380 --> 21:56.090
<i><b>Shooting Star Viewing</b></i>

21:58.320 --> 22:00.050
And this remote island...

22:00.050 --> 22:03.010
Nandan Island is famous
for its black sugar syrup!

22:03.010 --> 22:05.610
That's what really matters to you?!

22:06.400 --> 22:09.530
Today, at least, it would be nice
to have some sweet dreams.
